    "field": "Marine carbon cycle predictability",
    "problem": "While the physical state of the ocean is predictable years in advance, the decadal predictability of oceanic CO\u2082 uptake, a crucial component of the global carbon cycle, has remained unexplored in Earth system models.",
    "method": "The predictability of North Atlantic CO2 uptake is investigated by initializing an Earth System Model with assimilated physical ocean data and comparing decadal predictions against uninitialized simulations, an assimilation run, and observations to assess its potential multi-year predictive skill.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate the predictability of decadal variations in North Atlantic CO2 uptake using an initialized Earth system model and to demonstrate that its multi-year variability can be skillfully predicted up to 4\u20137 years in advance, primarily due to improved modeling of the ocean's physical state.",
