            "target_entity_instance": "root mean squared error",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "The initialized predictions produce ocean surface pCO2 closer to SOCAT observation than the uninitialized simulations as indicated by the correlations and root mean squared errors. The root mean squared error is lower in the assimilation and initialized simulations than in the uninitialized simulation.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": false,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "North Atlantic Oscillation",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "North Atlantic",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Consistent with previous model studies, the close connection between the NAO and the North Atlantic CO2 uptake at interannual and decadal timescales is also reproduced in the assimilation run.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Atlantic meridional overturning circulation",
            "source_entity_type": "Ocean_Circulation",
            "relation": "OBSERVED_IN_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "North Atlantic",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The variability of carbon uptake in the subpolar North Atlantic ocean was found to be largely related to variations of the North Atlantic Oscillation (NAO), the Atlantic meridional overturning circulation (AMOC), sea surface temperature (SST) and ocean-mixing strength, and all these processes are intrinsically related3,5\u20139.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
